const TeacherStudyData differentLandsTeacherStudy = TeacherStudyData(
  chapterSnapshot: 'Class 4 Environmental Studies & Social Studies chapter exploring how different landforms across India shape the way people live. Through four friends returning from vacation-Gurpreet (Amritsar plains), Ritika (Rajasthan desert), Chandni (Puri coastal region), and Nayan (Sikkim mountains)-the chapter examines how climate, terrain, and natural resources influence agriculture, water management, clothing, housing architecture, occupations, diet, and vibrant cultural traditions (Golden Temple Langar Seva, Rath Yatra, Odissi dance, sand art, Loosong/Namsoong festivals, and Chaam mask dance). Students also explore environmental challenges like cyclones in coastal zones and landslides on steep mountain slopes, culminating in a 4-region synthesis matrix.',
  learningOutcomes: [
    'Identify and describe the physical features of plains, deserts, coastal regions, and mountains.',
