    'Compare life across the four regions using trees, animals, houses, clothing, food, festivals, and art forms.',
    'Identify flora and fauna adapted to extreme environments (desert cactus, khejri, camel; mountain oak, pine, yak; coastal sea turtles, dolphins, corals).',
    'Describe specific architectural and water adaptations like desert tankas, mud walls, and mountain sloping wooden roofs.',
    'Explain natural hazards faced by communities (coastal cyclones and mountain landslides) and how preparedness protects lives.',
    'Connect geography with cultural expression by linking landforms to regional festivals, music, dance, and community services.',
